; vector-simple.scm (vector support): the function vector-safe-ref with vector-length and vector-ref
; expanded, as basic blocks, called from the top level with the literal #(1 2 3) and (read).
; The tests of the source are (fixnum? i) (A), (>= i 0) (B) and (< i (vector-length v)) (C, D);
; vector-ref then checks vector? (E), fixnum? (G), the lower bound (H) and the upper bound (J)
; before the access; every failed check goes to F.
; v is a vector of 3 elements: make-vector stands for the literal #(1 2 3). Inside vector-safe-ref,
; v is a parameter, so its length is the symbol of v and the checks are decided on that symbol.
function main()
M:  i = read()
    v = make-vector(3, 0)
    call vector-safe-ref(v, i) -> R
R:  return #res

function vector-safe-ref(v, i)
A:  if fixnum?(i) goto B else goto Z
B:  if >=(i, 0) goto C else goto Z
C:  if vector?(v) goto D else goto F
D:  len = ##vector-length(v)
    if <(i, len) goto E else goto Z
E:  if vector?(v) goto G else goto F
G:  if fixnum?(i) goto H else goto F
H:  if fx>=(i, 0) goto J else goto F
J:  len2 = ##vector-length(v)
    if fx<(i, len2) goto K else goto F
K:  return ##vector-ref(v, i)
Z:  return #f
F:  fail
